@page "/vanilla"

<PageTitle>Vanilla interop</PageTitle>
<h1>Vanilla interop</h1>
<p>A native InputText and ValidationMessage working beside a Formidable input in the same form — the css provider even gives the native input the same state classes.</p>

<TeachingPanel CodeFiles="@(new[] { "VanillaInterop.razor", "VanillaInterop.razor.cs", "GadgetOrder.cs" })">
    <Rules>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Nickname</strong> (a native <code>InputText</code>) — required, validated live.</li>
            <li><strong>Colour</strong> (a Formidable input) — required, validated live.</li>
            <li>The css provider gives native InputBase components the same state classes, so both inputs style identically with zero extra wiring.</li>
            <li>The rest is rendered by hand, one concern at a time: <code>FormidableFieldAnchor</code> registers it so its submit issues disclose, the field's own id on the input is what the summary's click-to-focus looks for, and <code>aria-describedby</code> plus <code>aria-invalid</code> give a screen reader the same message pairing and error state a Formidable input emits — the page reads that state off the engine, so it appears and clears with the message beside it.</li>
        </ul>
    </Rules>
    <TryIt>
        <ol>
            <li>Submit empty — both inputs show the identical red border.</li>
            <li>Click the <em>Nickname is required</em> entry in the summary — focus lands in the native input, just as the colour entry lands in the Formidable one. The focus service resolves a field to an element id and looks for nothing else, so a native input carrying that id is as reachable as a wrapped one.</li>
            <li>Note the native <code>ValidationMessage</code> and Formidable's <code>FormidableFieldMessage</code> rendering side by side.</li>
            <li>Fill both and submit — the status line confirms.</li>
        </ol>
    </TryIt>
</TeachingPanel>

<FormidableForm Model="_order" OnValidSubmit="HandleValid" @ref="_form">
    <div class="summary-slot">
        <FormidableSummary />
    </div>

    <div class="field">
        <label>Nickname (native InputText)
            <InputText @bind-Value="_order.Nickname"
                       id="@NicknameId"
                       aria-invalid="@NicknameAriaInvalid"
                       aria-describedby="@NicknameMessagesId" /></label>
        <ValidationMessage For="() => _order.Nickname" id="@NicknameMessagesId" />
        <FormidableFieldAnchor For="() => _order.Nickname" />
    </div>

    <div class="field">
        <label>Colour (Formidable input)
            <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_order.Colour" /></label>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _order.Colour" />
    </div>

    <div class="actions">
        <button type="submit">Submit</button>
    </div>
</FormidableForm>

<p role="status">@_status</p>
